==Strategy==
Although everything in this stage spawns on a timer, most of them are not to be trifled with. Red EnerG is the biggest threat here due to his surge attacks, so it would be wise to somehow eliminate him before he causes further trouble. The other enemies are mostly annoying, but you'll have to figure out how to deal with Oldhorn and Relic Doge in the meantime. The aliens can be a handful, too.

If you don't want to use the Breakerblast, bring something like [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] to deal with the UltraBaaBaas.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] - Deals high melee damage. With target alien and extra money talents it can even support your own economy well.
*[[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]]/[[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Future Cat]] - For countering the Relics that appear in this stage.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - An amazing unit with massive damage to Red enemies. Can be used to consistently chip Red EnerG.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Storm Beast Naala]] - Surge immune, strong against relics with a chance for weaken. Naala is a fairly risky play due to her low range, but her surge immunity is nothing to dismiss if you can get a stepping stone for her to snipe other enemies.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] - If you manage to obtain this unit's true form on 1 crown, he can work very well as he is surge immune and counters the Relic Enemies well.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]] - When talented, Greater Balrog boasts extreme DPS which is helpful for nuking frontline peons. Doesn't help against Red EnerG though.
*[[Jeanne (Legend Rare Cat)|Jeanne]] - If you're lucky enough to own this unit, you can use her to melt the Red EnerG, though it's just as risky as Naala due to her low health.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Yet another stage dominated by this Uber. Just bring something to break barriers and this stage will be a free one.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]]: A very fine pick for this stage thanks to his Alien and Relic targeting, knockback immunity, and barrier breaker.

